<article class="env-lemma" id="08AW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08AW">Lemma <span data-tag="08AW">69.22.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/08AV" data-tag="08AV">69.22.1</a>. Set $B = \bigoplus _{n \geq 0} I^ n$. Then for every $p \geq 0$ the graded $B$-module $\bigoplus _{n \geq 0} H^ p(X, I^ n\mathcal{F})$ is a finite $B$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{B} = \bigoplus I^ n\mathcal{O}_ X = f^*\widetilde{B}$. Then $\bigoplus I^ n\mathcal{F}$ is a finite type graded $\mathcal{B}$-module. Hence the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/08AT" data-tag="08AT">69.20.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>